Retain and reuse disconnected Bluetooth SPA devices, as WirePlumber 0.5.14 did.

0.5.18 creates a fresh SPA device for each connection event, but only stores it
once connected. Releasing the disconnected device clears PipeWire's device
settings before BAP SelectProperties, causing E to negotiate default LC3 QoS
and conversational context instead of its configured gaming context/preset.
Retain the device before activation and reuse it across connection transitions.
Signal handlers are installed only once, when the SPA device is first created.

Local fix against 0.5.18; remove when upstream restores equivalent lifetime.

